      label: 'Anther sits on the filament; the feathery one is the stigma',
      text: 'The classic label-the-flower question hinges on the stamen pair: the anther is the pollen sac, the filament is the stalk it sits on — don\'t swap them. The single most marked wind-pollination adaptation is the large feathery / exposed stigma (and exposed anthers on long filaments), which catch and release airborne pollen — that is what the visible feathery structure in the diagram is showing.',
