      prompt: 'In the Argand diagram above, write down z1, z2 and z3 in the form a + bi (a, b are integers), and state the value of |z2|.',
      modelAnswer: 'z1 = 4 + 3i (the point 4 across, 3 up). z2 = 0 + 2i, i.e. 2i (it lies on the imaginary axis, so the real part is 0). z3 = -2 - i (2 left, 1 down). |z2| = 2 (z2 sits 2 units up the imaginary axis, so its distance from the origin is 2).',
