    source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Mathematics 2024 Ordinary Level marking scheme, Paper 1 Q2(a): z1 = 4 + 3i, z2 = 0 + 2i (accept 2i), z3 = -2 - i, |z2| = 2.',
    marksWeight: 10,
    figure: { src: '/exam-figures/maths/mathematics-2024-ol-argand-diagram.png', alt: 'An Argand diagram with the real axis (Re) labelled from -4 to 5 and the imaginary axis (Im) labelled from -2 to 4 on a faint square grid. Three complex numbers are plotted as dots: z1 at 4 on the real axis and 3 on the imaginary axis, z2 on the imaginary axis at 2, and z3 at -2 on the real axis and -1 on the imaginary axis.', source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Mathematics 2024 Ordinary Level, Q2 — © State Examinations Commission' },
