    source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Biology 2021 Higher Level marking scheme, Q14(b)(ii)-(iii) — X = lacteal, role = to absorb (digested) fats / fatty acids; main function of villi = to increase surface area or for absorption (of nutrients); villi most abundant in small intestine/ileum; digested nutrients carried by hepatic portal vein to the liver',
    marksWeight: 9,
    figure: { src: '/exam-figures/biology/biology-2021-hl-villus.png', alt: 'A shaded longitudinal-section drawing of a single finger-like villus from the lining of the small intestine, with part of a neighbouring villus to its right. Three structures are labelled by leader arrows: \'Epithelium\' points to the thin single-cell dotted outer covering layer of the villus; \'X\' points to the central vessel running up the middle of the villus interior (the lacteal); and \'Blood capillary\' points to the branching, looping network of fine vessels surrounding the central lacteal inside the villus.', source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Biology 2021 Higher Level, Paper 2 Q14(b) — © State Examinations Commission' },
