      label: 'Name + describe + culinary example — all three or you cap the marks',
      text: 'Each property is marked in three parts: name (2), description (2) and culinary application (2). The 2024 HL scheme gives 6 marks per property only if you supply ALL three; a property described with no named dish (or a dish with no description) cannot reach full marks. Do not confuse caramelisation (sugar alone browning on heat) with the Maillard reaction (sugar PLUS amino acids/protein in dry heat) — the scheme treats them as distinct properties.',
