      needed: ['Infectious: bacteria produce endotoxins inside the cell, released when bacteria die', 'Endotoxins are easily destroyed by proper cooking/reheating; long incubation (over 12 hours)', 'Named infectious example (Salmonella / Listeria / E. coli / Campylobacter)', 'Toxic: bacteria produce exotoxins outside the cell, before and after the food is eaten', 'Exotoxins are hard to destroy (need ~30 min boiling); short incubation (about 2 hours)', 'Named toxic example (Staphylococcus aureus / Clostridium botulinum)'],
