    gist: 'Work in society is grouped into three types. PAID work is done for financial gain (wages/salary) — it can be full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or contract-based, employed or self-employed, and brings benefits like a pension, PRSI, holiday and sick pay. UNPAID work brings no financial reward — it includes domestic housework, child-rearing, caring for elderly or disabled family members, DIY, and work experience/placement. VOLUNTARY work means working for a community group or charity for no payment, to help others and make a difference in their lives.',
