    gist: 'Education plays two big roles in society. As a method of SOCIALISATION it passes on acceptable behaviour, cultural values and social skills — formally through the classroom/curriculum and informally through the \'hidden curriculum\' (punctuality, respect for authority, sharing, teamwork), reinforcing what is first taught at home. As PREPARATION FOR WORK it builds literacy and numeracy, formal qualifications and specialised skills, plus personal qualities like responsibility and self-discipline (with work experience through TY, LCA and LCVP). But access is not equal: socio-economic status affects equality of opportunity, because the cost of books, uniforms and equipment can be prohibitive for lower-income families.',
