      text: 'A part that reads \'Luaigh / Scríobh síos dhá phíosa eolais...\' is marked 3 + 2 = 5, so one fact, however good, can only earn 3. Count to two before you stop, and pick facts that don\'t overlap. For \'2.(b) Luaigh dhá phíosa eolais faoi cheolchoirm Ed Sheeran i bPáirc an Chrócaigh i mí Aibreáin. (Alt 2)\' Alt 2 hands you several clean facts in two sentences — more than 80,000 people were in Croke Park, it launched his world tour in April, the best of music could be heard, the atmosphere was incredible. Lift any two distinct ones, anchored to the exact line in the named alt. (Contrast 1(b) on Eilís II, a single 5-mark \'Cén fáth?\' — there one correct reason, e.g. that she was Queen for seventy years, already earns full marks, so don\'t over-write it.)',
