    gist: 'Enterprise and management overlap but are not the same. Enterprise is an attempt to take a personal and financial risk in order to create something new for the return of profit (the entrepreneur invests money, time and reputation in a new venture). Management is a goal-oriented process: co-ordinating the resources of an existing organisation to achieve its goals, using the skills (leading, motivating, communicating) and the activities (planning, organising, controlling). The same person can be both, but the entrepreneur creates and risks; the manager organises and delivers. Entrepreneurial skills/characteristics examiners reward include risk-taker, innovative, decision-making, identifying opportunities/spotting a gap, flexible and adaptable, human relations, and confident/self-motivated.',
