    gist: 'Leading is the management SKILL of guiding and directing staff so they work towards the business\'s goals. There are three leadership styles: Autocratic — the leader gives orders that are expected to be followed without question, does not consult or delegate, motivates by fear/intimidation, communication is one-way top-down. Democratic — the leader gives direction but consults staff, listens to opinions and suggestions, delegates to involve everyone, motivates by including and rewarding staff, communication is two-way. Laissez-faire (free-rein) — the leader has complete trust in employees, lets them make decisions with little direction, delegates almost all tasks and motivates by giving freedom.',
