    gist: 'Controlling is the management activity of checking that actual performance matches the plan and taking corrective action where it doesn\'t. The main types are: Stock control — holding the optimum level of stock (the right amount at the right time, not too much, not too little); Quality control — making sure products/service meet standards (inspections, quality circles, quality symbols, TQM); Financial control — using budgets and cashflow forecasts so short-term debts are paid on time and the business stays liquid; and Credit control — ensuring debtors pay promptly (credit checks, limits, interest/discounts) to avoid bad debts. Good control protects sales, cash and reputation.',
