    focus: 'Barriers to free trade', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'Free trade is buying and selling between countries with no government-imposed barriers. Governments sometimes block it to protect home industries (protectionism), using four classic barriers. TARIFF: a tax/customs duty on an import, raising its price to discourage consumption and protect home producers. QUOTA: a limit on the QUANTITY (number of items) of a good that may be imported in a period. SUBSIDY: financial support a government gives a domestic industry to lower its costs so it can undercut imports. EMBARGO: a total ban on the import of certain goods from certain countries. The World Trade Organisation (WTO) works to remove these so trade flows as freely as possible.',
