    focus: 'Relevez / Citez / Trouvez — lift the exact words', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'When a reading question starts with Relevez (pick out), Citez (quote) or Trouvez (find), the examiner wants you to COPY the exact words from the text — do not reword, do not explain, do not add. Relevez / Citez = \'find and write back the words that are already there\'. So if the question says \'Citez l\'expression qui veut dire...\' (quote the expression that means...), you hunt the section for the synonym and write that phrase out word for word. Trap: copying too little (you drop the word that carries the meaning) or copying too much (the scheme docks marks for excess / extraneous words). The trick is to copy the WHOLE expression — no more, no less.',
