    focus: 'Answering in the right language (French vs English/Irish)', level: 'common',
    gist: 'Every French comprehension answer must be written in the language the rubric demands — and it changes between sections, so read the instruction line, not just the question. Rule of thumb: if the question is printed in FRENCH, answer in French; if it is printed in IRISH/ENGLISH, answer in Irish/English. Two big consequences: (1) At Higher Level the Reading Comprehension questions in French are answered in French (the 2024 HL paper says so explicitly: \'Aux autres questions en français, il faut répondre en français\'). (2) At BOTH levels the Listening (Aural) test is answered in English/Irish — even at HL — and Ordinary Level Reading questions are printed in Irish/English too. Writing the right content in the wrong language throws away marks you already earned.',
