      text: 'The LC French HL Listening paper (2024) states plainly: \'Questions to be answered in English\'. The HL marking scheme has a named penalty \'Penalty for Listening Comprehension answered in French\', and the Listening section instructs: if a whole section is answered in French, mark it then DEDUCT 50% of the marks gained. HL Reading is the opposite — answer in French, and the Reading penalties list flags \'answers in Irish/English when French required\'. At Ordinary Level the Reading is printed in Irish/English with \'ANSWER IN ENGLISH\', so English is correct there. Before you write a word, glance at the section\'s instruction line and match its language.',
