    gist: 'In terms of electrons: oxidation is the LOSS of electrons and reduction is the GAIN of electrons — remember OIL RIG (Oxidation Is Loss, Reduction Is Gain). A redox reaction has both happening at once. When zinc is dropped into blue copper(II) sulfate solution, zinc loses electrons (it is oxidised) and copper ions gain them (they are reduced): Zn loses 2 electrons to become Zn2+, and Cu2+ gains those 2 electrons to become Cu metal. The reducing agent is the substance that hands over electrons — here, the zinc.',
