      modelAnswer: '(i) Oxidation is the loss of electrons. (ii) The copper half-equation (Cu2+ + 2e- -> Cu) is a reduction, because the Cu2+ ions gain electrons. (iii) Zinc is the reducing agent — it loses electrons (is oxidised) and so supplies the electrons that reduce the copper ions.',
