    focus: 'Rate from a graph + average rate', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'Rate of reaction = the change in concentration (or amount) of a substance per unit time. You measure it by following something that changes as the reaction goes — here, the volume of O2 gas collected in a gas syringe as hydrogen peroxide (H2O2) breaks down on a manganese dioxide (MnO2) catalyst. Plot volume of gas against time and you get a curve that is STEEP at the start (fast) and FLATTENS at the end (slow), levelling off when the reaction finishes. The reaction slows as it goes because the reactant (H2O2) is being used up, so its concentration keeps dropping. The AVERAGE rate over a time interval is just total change in volume divided by the time taken.',
