      modelAnswer: '(a) Rate of reaction = the change in concentration of a reactant or product per unit time (a measure of how fast the reaction goes). (b) Average rate = change in volume ÷ time = 48 ÷ 4 = 12 cm³ min⁻¹. (c) The H2O2 (reactant) is being used up, so its concentration decreases as the reaction proceeds — fewer collisions per second — so the rate falls and the curve flattens.',
