    id: 'chem-reaction-heat-combustion',
    subjectId: 'chemistry', topicId: 'chemistry-6-2',
    subjectLabel: 'Chemistry', topicLabel: 'Organic Reaction Types',
    focus: 'Heat of combustion of an alkane (Hess\'s law)', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'Combustion is the organic reaction type behind heat-of-combustion calculations. You find it from heats of formation using: dH(reaction) = sum of dH(formation) of products - sum of dH(formation) of reactants. Multiply each substance\'s heat of formation by its number in the balanced equation, keep the minus signs, then subtract the reactants total. Elements like O2 have a heat of formation of zero. Worked example (octane): for CH3(CH2)6CH3(l) + 12.5 O2(g) -> 8CO2(g) + 9H2O(l), with dHf(octane) = -250.3, dHf(CO2) = -393.5 and dHf(H2O) = -285.8 kJ/mol: products = 8(-393.5) + 9(-285.8) = -3148 + (-2572.2) = -5720.2; subtract the reactant = -5720.2 - (-250.3) = -5469.9 kJ/mol.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Products minus reactants, sign of every term, then sense-check it\'s exothermic',
      text: 'The 2024 HL Q6(d)(i) scheme awards each term separately: marks for the multiplicative factor AND a mark for the sign of each of the three terms (8 x -393.5, 9 x -285.8, and -(-250.3)). So the easiest marks to drop are sign slips: products carry their NEGATIVE values, and you SUBTRACT the reactant, which flips -250.3 into +250.3. Combustion must come out negative (exothermic) - if your answer is positive you\'ve made a sign error.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'For the complete combustion of octane:  CH3(CH2)6CH3(l) + 12.5 O2(g) -> 8 CO2(g) + 9 H2O(l). The heat of formation of octane is -250.3 kJ/mol; of CO2 is -393.5 kJ/mol; of H2O is -285.8 kJ/mol (O2 = 0). Calculate the heat of combustion of octane in kJ/mol.',
      modelAnswer: 'dHc = [8(-393.5) + 9(-285.8)] - [(-250.3)] = [-3148 + (-2572.2)] - (-250.3) = -5720.2 + 250.3 = -5469.9 kJ/mol.',
      needed: ['Products: 8(-393.5) + 9(-285.8) = -5720.2', 'Subtract reactant: -(-250.3) = +250.3', 'Final answer -5469.9 kJ/mol (negative / exothermic)'],
    },
    source: 'Organic Chemistry 7.3 Organic Reaction Types - SEC LC Chemistry 2024 Higher Level Q6(d)(i) (marking scheme: 8(-393.5), 9(-285.8), -(-250.3) each scored for multiplicative factor + sign; = -5469.9 kJ/mol)',
    marksWeight: 14,
