    gist: 'Total hardness = the sum of all dissolved Ca2+ and Mg2+ ions (temporary + permanent), and it is measured by titrating a known volume of the water against a standard EDTA solution using Solochrome Black (Eriochrome Black T) indicator, with a buffer holding the mixture at pH 10. EDTA reacts with the hardness ions 1:1 (M2+ + H2Y2- -> MY2- + 2H+). At the end point the colour changes from wine-red to blue. The result is converted to a concentration of CaCO3 (g per litre, then to p.p.m.).',
