      text: 'The equation is 1:1, so moles of M2+ = moles of EDTA. Each conversion step earns its own 3 marks in the 2022 HL scheme, so SHOW every line: (1) moles EDTA = (volume in cm3 x molarity)/1000; (2) moles M2+ = same number (1:1); (3) scale a 25.0 cm3 sample up to 1 litre by x40; (4) x100 (the Mr of CaCO3) to get g/L; (5) x1000 to get p.p.m. The scheme flags \'Multiply by 40 essential\' and \'Multiply by 100 essential\' - skipping the \'x40 to a litre\' step or the \'x100 as CaCO3\' step is the classic mark-loser.',
