    focus: 'Latent heat of fusion: full energy balance', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'The HL latent-heat-of-fusion experiment is a four-term energy balance, and that is exactly where marks bleed away. The warm water and the copper calorimeter both lose heat; the ice both melts (ml) AND the melted ice then warms from 0 C up to the final temperature. Students who forget that fourth term (the melted ice warming up) get the wrong l. The scheme awards the formula and each mass/temperature read-off separately, so set out every term before you plug in numbers.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Write the full balance with all four terms',
      text: 'Heat LOST = Heat GAINED. Lost = (mc dtheta)_water + (mc dtheta)_calorimeter. Gained = (ml)_ice + (mc dtheta)_melted-ice, where the melted ice warms from 0 C to the FINAL temperature. The single most common mark-loss is dropping the (mc dtheta)_melted-ice term. Get masses by subtraction first: m_water = 132.9 - 83.2 = 49.7 g, m_ice = 138.5 - 132.9 = 5.6 g.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'In a latent-heat-of-fusion experiment: copper calorimeter = 83.2 g; calorimeter + water before adding ice = 132.9 g; after adding ice = 138.5 g; water temperature falls from 26.8 C to 17.4 C. Using c_water = 4180 J kg^-1 K^-1 and c_copper = 390 J kg^-1 K^-1, calculate (a) the energy lost by the copper calorimeter, and (b) the specific latent heat of fusion of ice, l.',
      modelAnswer: 'Masses by subtraction: m_water = 132.9 - 83.2 = 49.7 g = 0.0497 kg; m_ice = 138.5 - 132.9 = 5.6 g = 0.0056 kg; m_cal = 83.2 g = 0.0832 kg. Temperature drop dtheta = 26.8 - 17.4 = 9.4 C.\n(a) Energy lost by calorimeter = mc dtheta = 0.0832 x 390 x 9.4 = 305 J.\n(b) Energy balance: (ml)_ice + (mc dtheta)_melted-ice = (mc dtheta)_water + (mc dtheta)_calorimeter.\nEnergy lost by water = 0.0497 x 4180 x 9.4 = 1953 J. Total energy lost = 1953 + 305 = 2258 J.\nMelted ice (now water) warms from 0 C to 17.4 C: 0.0056 x 4180 x 17.4 = 407 J.\nSo (m l)_ice = 2258 - 407 = 1851 J. l = 1851 / 0.0056 = 3.3 x 10^5 J kg^-1.',
      needed: ['energy lost by calorimeter mc dtheta = 0.0832 x 390 x 9.4 = 305 J', 'full balance (ml)_ice + (mc dtheta)_melted-ice = (mc dtheta)_water + (mc dtheta)_calorimeter', 'l = 3.3 x 10^5 J kg^-1'],
    },
    source: 'Specific latent heat of fusion of ice (experiment) - SEC LC Physics 2024 Higher, Q3(iii),(iv) + marking scheme (energy lost by calorimeter = 305 J; l = 3.3 x 10^5 J kg^-1)',
