    focus: 'Doppler: moving (falling) source calc', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'HL Doppler calculations almost always hide a first step: you must find the source speed yourself before using the Doppler formula. In the 2022 falling-toy question the toy is dropped, so u = v = u_0 + at gives its speed after 3 s, and only THEN do you apply f\' = fc / (c +/- u). Because the source is falling AWAY from the listener at the top, the apparent frequency drops, so you must ADD u to c in the denominator. Pick the wrong sign and the whole answer is wrong even though the method looks right.',
