    focus: 'Critical angle to speed of light in glass', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'Two formulae chain together here: n = 1/sin C links the critical angle to refractive index, and n = c1/c2 links refractive index to the speed of light in the medium. The exam gives only the critical angle and asks for the speed in the glass, so you must use the first to find n and then the second to find c2. The common error is stopping at n, or trying to use sin C directly in a speed formula.',
