    gist: 'The resistivity experiment is one of the most reliably examined HL practicals. After you find the wire\'s resistance R from the slope of your V-I graph, the last marks come from rho = RA/l. The two places students drop marks: forgetting that A is the cross-sectional AREA (you must turn diameter into radius, halve it, then use pi*r^2), and not converting cm and mm to metres. Get the formula and the area down and the marks are yours even if your R was slightly off.',
