    focus: 'Fission: control rods/moderator + half-life fraction + alpha daughter', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'The nuclear fission question is mostly recall plus two short calculations. The recall marks (what fission is, what control rods and the moderator do, what isotopes are) are easy to bank if you keep the two component roles straight: control rods ABSORB neutrons, the moderator SLOWS DOWN neutrons. Students mix these two up and lose half the marks. The \'fraction remaining\' part is a half-life count, and the daughter-nucleus part just needs the mass and atomic numbers to balance.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Keep control rods (absorb) and moderator (slow down) separate, and count half-lives as a fraction',
      text: 'Lock in the two roles: control rods ABSORB neutrons (to control the chain reaction), the moderator SLOWS DOWN neutrons (so they cause more fission). For \'fraction remaining after 72330 years\' with half-life 24110 years: 72330 / 24110 = 3 half-lives, so the fraction is (1/2)^3 = 1/8. For the alpha-decay daughter, balance the numbers - an alpha is (4,2)He, so subtract 4 from the mass number (239 -> 235) and 2 from the atomic number (94 -> 92), and Z=92 is uranium: the daughter is (235,92)U.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: '(i) What is the function of (a) the control rods and (b) the moderator in a nuclear fission reactor? (ii) Pu-239 has a half-life of 24110 years. What fraction of the isotope will remain after 72330 years? (iii) Plutonium decays by alpha emission: (239,94)Pu -> X + (4,2)alpha. Identify the daughter nucleus X. (Z=92 is uranium.)',
      modelAnswer: '(i)(a) Control rods absorb neutrons (controlling the rate of the chain reaction). (b) The moderator slows down neutrons (so they are more likely to cause further fission).\n(ii) Number of half-lives = 72330 / 24110 = 3. Fraction remaining = (1/2)^3 = 1/8.\n(iii) An alpha particle is (4,2)He. Balancing the equation: mass number 239 - 4 = 235; atomic number 94 - 2 = 92. Z=92 is uranium, so the daughter nucleus is (235,92)U.',
      needed: ['Control rods absorb neutrons; moderator slows down neutrons (not interchanged)', '72330 / 24110 = 3 half-lives, so fraction remaining = 1/8', 'Daughter nucleus is (235,92)U (mass 235, atomic number 92, uranium)'],
    },
    source: 'Nuclear Energy / Fission - SEC LC Physics 2024 Ordinary, Q12(ii),(v),(vi) + marking scheme (control rods absorb / moderator slows neutrons; fraction = 1/8; daughter = (235,92)U)',
