    gist: 'This radioactivity question tests whether you can read a nuclear symbol and balance an alpha decay. The notation (226,88)Ra means mass number 226 (top) and atomic number 88 (bottom). Neutrons = mass number minus atomic number. Students lose marks by subtracting the wrong way, or by forgetting that emitting TWO alpha particles changes the numbers twice. Each alpha is (4,2)He, so each one drops the mass by 4 and the atomic number by 2.',
