      label: 'Closed pipe fits lambda/4, not lambda/2',
      text: 'For a pipe closed at one end at its fundamental, the standing wave is a node at the closed end and an antinode at the open end -> only a quarter wavelength fits, so length = lambda/4. Work it in two steps: lambda = c/f = 336/320 = 1.05 m, then l = lambda/4 = 1.05/4 = 0.26 m. Don\'t reuse the open-pipe/string rule (lambda/2) here -- that doubles your pipe length and loses the marks.',
