    gist: 'DBQ Question 1 is comprehension (20 marks, four parts at 5M each on the HL paper). It is not asking for your opinion or background knowledge - it asks what a NAMED document actually states. The scheme awards the mark only for the specific point the document gives, so the killer error is paraphrasing vaguely or answering from outside knowledge. Go to the named document, find the line that answers the exact word in the question, and lift that point.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Answer FROM the named document, in its own words',
      text: 'For each part the question names a document (\'According to document A...\'). Re-read that document only, find the sentence that matches the question word for word, and state that exact point - quoting or closely echoing the document. Do not generalise (\'there were problems\') and do not add background you know from class: the scheme awards the precise stated fact, nothing else.',
    },
