      modelAnswer: '(a) The Soviet authorities had established the existence of a large terrorist conspiracy against the Party leaders, including Stalin. (b) The Soviet government had no choice but to take tough measures against the plotters - that is, to shoot the 80-100 people involved. Each answer is lifted straight from document A in its own wording, not from outside knowledge.',
      needed: ['(a) a (large) terrorist conspiracy against the Party leaders / Stalin - the exact point document A states', '(b) to take tough measures against the plotters / to execute the 80-100 people - the only option the document gives', 'the answer is taken from the wording of document A, not from general background'],
