    gist: 'An HL essay is NOT marked by length or by how much of the topic you know. The examiner splits your answer into paragraphs and counts Cumulative Marks (CM, max 60) for content that is accurate AND relevant to the exact question, then adds an Overall Evaluation (OE, max 40) for analysis and judgement. A \'Significant Relevant Statement\' (SRS) is one distinct, accurate point that actually addresses the question. Narration that drifts off the question earns almost nothing, no matter how true it is - so relevance, not recall, is the real skill.',
