    focus: 'Positive externality: identify a spillover benefit (vaccination)', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'An externality is an external cost or benefit that falls on OTHER people or society as a result of someone\'s production or consumption. Vaccination is the classic POSITIVE externality: when you get vaccinated, OTHER people benefit too (less spread, less pressure on hospitals). The 2022 OL paper asked for an example of this spillover benefit and an opportunity cost of the government providing it.',
