    id: 'econ-gdp-to-gnp-nfia-calc-2023-hl',
    subjectId: 'economics', topicId: 'economics-3-0',
    subjectLabel: 'Economics', topicLabel: 'National Income (GDP, GNP, GNI)',
    focus: 'GDP -> GNP via net factor income from abroad', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'The national-income measures form a chain. GNP = GDP + net factor income from abroad (NFIA). For Ireland NFIA is large and NEGATIVE (profits/income flow OUT to foreign-owned multinationals), so GNP is well BELOW GDP. Then GNI = GNP + EU subsidies - EU taxes, and Modified GNI (GNI*) strips out distorting items (redomiciled firms\' income, depreciation on IP and aircraft leasing) to show the real domestic economy. Examiners give you GDP plus a table and ask you to work down the chain.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'GNP = GDP minus net factor income (NFIA is negative for Ireland)',
      text: 'Add NFIA to GDP with its SIGN. Because Ireland\'s NFIA is negative (income earned by foreign multinationals leaves the country), you SUBTRACT it, so GNP < GDP. The classic error is adding the EUR103bn instead of subtracting it, or adding EU taxes / subtracting EU subsidies the wrong way round. Keep the order: GDP -> (+/- NFIA) -> GNP -> (+EU subsidies, -EU taxes) -> GNI -> (- adjustments) -> Modified GNI.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'GDP at Current Market Prices is EUR426bn. Net factor income from abroad is -EUR103bn, EU subsidies are EUR1.7bn, EU taxes are EUR0.5bn, and the adjustments (factor income of redomiciled companies, depreciation on R&D/IP imports and aircraft leasing) total EUR89bn. Calculate, in order, (a) GNP at CMP, (b) Gross National Income at CMP, and (c) Modified Gross National Income at CMP. State each relationship.',
      modelAnswer: '(a) GNP = GDP + NFIA = 426 + (-103) = EUR323bn (NFIA is negative for Ireland, so GNP is below GDP). (b) GNI = GNP + EU subsidies - EU taxes = 323 + 1.7 - 0.5 = EUR324.2bn. (c) Modified GNI (GNI*) = GNI - adjustments = 324.2 - 89 = EUR235.2bn. The large gap between GDP (426) and Modified GNI (235.2) reflects the distortion from foreign-owned multinational activity in Ireland.',
      needed: ['GNP = GDP + NFIA = 426 + (-103) = EUR323bn (subtract because NFIA is negative)', 'GNI = GNP + EU subsidies - EU taxes = 323 + 1.7 - 0.5 = EUR324.2bn', 'Modified GNI = GNI - adjustments = 324.2 - 89 = EUR235.2bn'],
    },
    source: 'Topic National Income (GDP/GNP/GNI) — SEC LC Economics 2023 Higher, Q (GDP at CMP EUR426bn; calculate B and C) + marking scheme (GNP = EUR323bn; GNI = 323 + 1.7 - 0.5 = EUR324.2bn; Modified GNI = 324.2 - 89 = EUR235.2bn)',
    marksWeight: 12,
