    focus: 'Factors affecting demand (non-price)', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'Demand is how much of a good consumers are willing and able to buy. Price is only one thing that moves it. When a question says \'other than price\', it wants a SEPARATE factor that shifts demand: consumer income, tastes and preferences, the price of substitutes or complements, or seasonal/expectations factors. The marks come from naming a real factor AND saying which way it pushes demand (up or down) and why.',
