    gist: 'Soil pH controls nutrient availability, so liming is one of the most reliably examined soil topics. The single fact students lose marks on is the direction: lime RAISES soil pH (corrects acidity), it does not lower it. The optimum pH range for most crops is about 5.5-7.5. Liming also brings knock-on benefits (more earthworm activity, better structure, higher cation exchange capacity, better nutrient availability) and lowers nitrous oxide (N2O) emissions, which the exam links to sustainability.',
