    gist: 'Establishment questions reward precise definitions of sowing methods. Direct drilling means the seed is placed straight into the stubble/soil WITHOUT any prior cultivation (no ploughing) - which protects soil structure and organic matter. Undersowing means sowing two crops together so the second crop continues growing after the first is harvested. A clover companion crop fixes nitrogen and improves soil. The exam asks you to explain the underlined term AND give a specific advantage.',
