    gist: 'Making good first-cut silage is a sequence: cut at the leafy (vegetative) stage in May/early June for high sugar and digestibility, after spreading fertiliser 6-8 weeks earlier; then wilt, harvest, pack tightly to remove air (anaerobic), and seal. You may also be asked to calculate Dry Matter percentage from a fresh and a dried sample weight. DM% = (dried weight / fresh weight) x 100.',
