      text: 'For Dry Matter %, divide the DRIED (oven-dried) weight by the FRESH weight and multiply by 100 - do NOT subtract or invert it. e.g. 37 g dried / 124 g fresh x 100 = 29.83%. And for the silage steps, the highest-value point is cutting at the LEAFY (vegetative) stage, because that is when sugar and digestibility (DMD) are highest for fermentation.',
