      label: 'The MORE FREQUENT offspring phenotype is the dominant trait (look for the ~3:1)',
      text: 'Do not pick dominant by appearance — pick it by COUNT. With 14 purple : 6 white offspring, purple is far more common (14:6 simplifies to 7:3, close to the expected 3:1 monohybrid ratio), so PURPLE is the dominant trait and white is recessive. Then state the farm use: knowledge of genetic inheritance lets a grower SELECT for beneficial traits (yield, disease resistance, earliness of ripening) to improve crop production.',
