      modelAnswer: '(i) Purple is the dominant trait. Of the 20 offspring, 14 are purple and only 6 are white; purple appears in much the greater proportion (14:6, i.e. about 7:3, close to the expected 3:1 ratio of a monohybrid cross), so the trait shown by the majority — purple — is dominant and white is recessive. (ii) Knowing how traits are inherited lets the grower select and breed plants carrying beneficial traits — such as high yield, disease resistance, or earliness of ripening — improving the quality and output of the tillage crop over successive generations.',
