    id: 'acc-incomplete-records-credit-purchases-creditors-control-hl',
    subjectId: 'accounting', topicId: 'accounting-6-1',
    subjectLabel: 'Accounting', topicLabel: 'Incomplete Records',
    focus: 'Credit purchases via the creditors control account (balancing figure)', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'In incomplete-records questions the purchases figure is missing, so you reconstruct it from a creditors (purchases ledger) control account. The cash/bank paid to creditors and the opening and closing creditor balances are known; credit purchases is the balancing figure. The accounting logic: opening creditors + credit purchases = payments to creditors + closing creditors, so credit purchases = payments + closing creditors - opening creditors. The same control-account technique finds credit sales from a debtors control account.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Credit purchases = payments + closing creditors - opening creditors',
      text: 'Set up the creditors control account: CREDIT side = opening creditors balance b/d + credit purchases (the missing figure); DEBIT side = bank/cash paid to creditors + closing creditors balance c/d. Credit purchases is the figure that makes both sides balance. The most common error is reversing the opening/closing balances - the OPENING balance is on the credit (brought-down) side, the CLOSING balance is on the debit (carried-down) side.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'P. Shepard kept no full set of books for 2022. Trade creditors: 01/01/2022 (opening) 57,700; 31/12/2022 (closing) 55,400. Bank payments to creditors during the year were 37,000. There are no other items affecting the creditors account (no contras or returns). Using a creditors control account, calculate the credit purchases for the year.',
      modelAnswer: 'Creditors control account: credit side = opening balance b/d 57,700 + credit purchases (balancing figure). Debit side = bank paid 37,000 + closing balance c/d 55,400 = 92,400. Credit purchases = 92,400 - 57,700 = 34,700. Check with the formula: credit purchases = payments 37,000 + closing creditors 55,400 - opening creditors 57,700 = 34,700.',
      needed: ['Opening creditors 57,700 on the credit (b/d) side; closing creditors 55,400 on the debit (c/d) side', 'Credit purchases = 37,000 + 55,400 - 57,700 = 34,700 as the balancing figure', 'Stated formula: credit purchases = payments to creditors + closing creditors - opening creditors'],
    },
    source: 'Topic 6.1 Incomplete Records (Final Accounts via Control Accounts) - SEC LC Accounting 2023 Higher Level, Q2 + marking scheme W2 Purchases (Credit: 37,000 + 55,400 - 57,700 = 34,700)',
