    id: 'es-a-personal-hl',
    subjectId: 'spanish', topicId: 'spanish-1-3',
    subjectLabel: 'Spanish', topicLabel: 'The personal \'a\'',
    focus: 'Personal \'a\' before a specific human direct object', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'Spanish puts a small \'a\' before a direct object that is a SPECIFIC PERSON (or a pet/personified thing) — there is no English equivalent, so it is easy to drop and lose Language-band polish in written production. \'Veo la casa\' (I see the house) — a thing, no \'a\' — but \'Veo a mi hermana\' (I see my sister) — a specific person, so \'a\' is required. The 2024 HL aural\'s Question 2 interview was about a host, Charo López, who welcomes women travellers into her home, so you could write \'Recibe a las viajeras en su casa\' (She welcomes the travellers into her home) — \'a\' before the specific people. With \'a + el\' it always contracts to \'al\': \'Llamé al profesor\' (I called the teacher). It drops with \'tener\': \'Tengo dos hermanos\' (no personal \'a\').',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Insert \'a\' before a specific human object',
      text: 'When the direct object is a particular person, insert the personal \'a\': write \'Ayudo a mi madre\' (I help my mother), \'Conocí a Pablo\' (I met Pablo), NOT \'Ayudo mi madre\'. Remember \'a + el = al\' (\'Visité al médico\') and that \'tener\' does not take it (\'Tengo un amigo\').',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'Add the personal \'a\' if it is needed, and explain: (1) \'Llevé ____ mi hermano al cine.\' (2) \'Compré ____ un billete de tren.\'',
      modelAnswer: '(1) \'Llevé a mi hermano al cine\' (I took my brother to the cinema) — the direct object \'mi hermano\' is a specific person, so the personal \'a\' is required. (2) \'Compré un billete de tren\' (I bought a train ticket) — no \'a\', because the direct object is a thing, not a person.',
      needed: ['Personal \'a\' added in (1) because \'mi hermano\' is a specific human direct object', 'No \'a\' in (2) because the object is a thing, with the reason that the personal \'a\' marks only people'],
    },
    source: 'Topic Writing About Your Experience — SEC LC Spanish 2024 HL aural Question 2 (interview with Charo López, \'ANFITRIONA DE VIAJERAS\', who hosts women travellers in her home), the kind of personal-object writing tested in Section C Written Production (50 marks; verbs/accuracy required for full marks)',
    marksWeight: 50,
