    id: 'es-gustar-agreement-ol',
    subjectId: 'spanish', topicId: 'spanish-1-3',
    subjectLabel: 'Spanish', topicLabel: 'Gustar-type verbs',
    focus: 'me gusta vs me gustan — verb agrees with the thing liked', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'In the Section B letter (40 marks) tasks like \'Mention two things you like about school\' and \'Give your opinion on Spanish food\' (2025 OL) need \'gustar\'. Gustar works backwards: the THING liked is the subject, so the verb agrees with IT, not with you. ONE thing -> \'me gusta\' (\'me gusta el español\' = I like Spanish); MORE THAN ONE thing -> \'me gustan\' (\'me gustan los deportes\' = I like sports). Before an action (infinitive) always use the singular: \'me gusta bailar\' (I like to dance). Same pattern with \'encanta/encantan\', \'interesa/interesan\': the 2025 OL text shows \'Me encanta la idea\' (singular thing).',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Match gusta/gustan to the thing, not to \'I\'',
      text: 'Make the verb agree with WHAT is liked: \'me gustaN los gatos\' (I like cats — plural thing -> gustan), but \'me gustA el chocolate\' (I like chocolate — singular thing -> gusta). For another person use the right pronoun: \'le gusta el fútbol\' (he/she likes football). With a verb, stay singular: \'me gusta nadar\' (I like to swim).',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'Fill in \'gusta\' or \'gustan\': (1) \'Me ____ las películas españolas.\' (2) \'A mi hermano le ____ el cine.\'',
      modelAnswer: '(1) \'Me GUSTAN las películas españolas\' (I like Spanish films) — \'las películas\' is plural, so the verb is plural. (2) \'A mi hermano le GUSTA el cine\' (My brother likes cinema) — \'el cine\' is singular, and \'le\' is the pronoun for \'he\', so the verb is singular \'gusta\'.',
      needed: ['\'gustan\' in (1) because the liked thing \'las películas\' is plural', '\'gusta\' in (2) because \'el cine\' is singular, plus correct use of \'le\' for a third person'],
    },
    source: 'Topic Writing About Your Experience — SEC LC Spanish 2025 OL, Section B Q1 letter (\'Mention two things you like about school\'; \'Give him your opinion on Spanish food\', 40 marks) + 2025 OL reading text \'Me encanta la idea\'',
