    subjectId: 'spanish', topicId: 'spanish-1-3',
    subjectLabel: 'Spanish', topicLabel: 'Section C dialogue: verb accuracy per turn',
    focus: 'Section C dialogue: 6 marks/turn needs the verb correct, in the right tense', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'Section C Q1(a) Dialogue Construction (30 marks) gives English instructions for five \'turns\' worth 6 marks each, and the scheme is blunt: \'Verbs must be correct for full marks.\' A turn whose message gets across but whose verb is wrong drops to the 4-5 band. The English cue tells you the tense: \'Say that your sister DID Erasmus three years ago\' = preterite (hizo); \'Tell him that\'s great news, you ARE delighted\' = present (estás encantado/a); \'Ask him WHERE he\'s planning to study\' = present with the question word (¿Dónde piensas estudiar?). Match the tense the cue signals before you worry about anything else.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Read the tense out of the English cue, then conjugate that exact verb',
      text: 'Each cue carries a tense flag: a past time-marker (\'three years ago\', \'last weekend\') = preterite (mi hermana HIZO Erasmus, not \'hace\'); \'is/are\' = present (estoy encantado/a); \'will / is going to\' = future or ir a + infinitive (voy a comprar); \'would love\' = conditional (me encantaría). Conjugate THAT verb for the subject named in the cue (your sister = 3rd person hizo, disfrutó). A right message wrapped around a wrong-tense or unconjugated verb costs you the gap between 6 and 4-5 on that turn.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'The dialogue cue is: \'Say that your sister did Erasmus in Austria three years ago, she enjoyed the experience and made friends.\' Write the Spanish, and name the tense each verb must be in.',
      modelAnswer: '\'Mi hermana hizo Erasmus en Austria hace tres años, disfrutó de la experiencia e hizo amigos.\' All three verbs are in the PRETERITE because \'hace tres años\' (three years ago) marks a completed past event: hizo (hacer, 3rd sing.), disfrutó (disfrutar), hizo amigos (made friends). Note \'e hizo\' not \'y hizo\' — y becomes e before an i-sound. Correct preterite verbs here secure the full 6 marks for the turn; a present-tense \'hace\' or unconjugated verb drops it to the 4-5 band.',
      needed: ['All verbs in the preterite (hizo, disfrutó, hizo amigos) because \'hace tres años\' is a completed past', 'Correct 3rd-person-singular agreement for \'my sister\'', '\'e hizo\' (e not y before an i-sound), and the link to \'verbs must be correct for full marks\''],
    },
    source: 'Topic: Written production dialogue construction — SEC LC Spanish 2025 HL, Section C Q1(a) Dialogue Construction (30 marks, 5 turns x 6m; cue \'Say that your sister did Erasmus in Austria three years ago...\') + marking scheme (\'Verbs must be correct for full marks\'; 6 marks = \'Communicative intention fulfilled\')',
    marksWeight: 30,
