    focus: 'Literature comprehension: copy the EXACT synonym from the text', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'In Q1(a) Prescribed Literature (Relato de un náufrago) the first sub-question gives you English-glossed words and asks you to FIND and COPY the matching word or phrase from the passage (e.g. it gives \'aguantar\' [to endure] and the text contains \'soportando\'; it gives \'extraño\' [strange] and the text says \'un animal raro\'; \'recuperado\' [recovered] matches \'restablecido\'). This is a vocabulary-matching transcription task, not a translation. The scheme is brutal: copy the word LETTER-FOR-LETTER and ACCENT-FOR-ACCENT. These are 9 easy marks (3 x 3m) that students throw away by paraphrasing or grabbing a whole clause.',
