    focus: 'Literature \'Discuss\' (Q5): answer in your OWN words, no quoting', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'The last literature sub-question is an inference/discussion task worth 12 marks (4+4+4) — e.g. \'Throughout his time adrift Luis alternates between hope and despair. Discuss.\' It is answered in ENGLISH and the paper warns \'You may not support your answer by reference to the extract.\' The scheme confirms: \'[No marks awarded for answers supported by reference to the extract].\' So you must make THREE separate points in your own English words, each a genuine interpretation — not a copied or translated Spanish phrase. Students who quote the text or just retell the plot lose all 12 marks even though they \'used the text\'.',
