      text: 'For each of the three requirements, write the heading then two lines: what the wall must achieve and the construction detail that delivers it. Structural stability = spread floor/roof loads evenly onto the foundation and resist cracking. Thermal comfort = carry insulation (and thermal mass) to keep heat in. Weather resistance = keep out wind-driven rain via render and a DPC, with no cold bridges or condensation. A bare list of headings with no \'how\' scores the label mark only and forfeits the explanation marks.',
