      modelAnswer: '1) Structural stability: the wall must spread the superimposed floor and roof loads evenly onto the foundation and resist cracking under load; achieved by load-bearing blockwork/leaves with robust lintels over openings. 2) Thermal comfort: the wall must limit heat loss to keep the interior warm; achieved by installing insulation (full-fill cavity or external insulation) and using thermal mass on the inner leaf. 3) Weather resistance: the wall must keep out wind-driven rain and prevent dampness/condensation; achieved by an external render finish, a damp-proof course in the rising wall and avoidance of cold bridges. (Fire resistance — withstand fire for at least 30 minutes before structural integrity is lost — and acoustic resistance are also accepted.)',
