      modelAnswer: '(a) The wall tie is bedded into both block leaves and slopes slightly DOWNWARD towards the outer leaf, with a drip at the lowest point, so that any moisture that tracks along the tie runs out to the outer leaf and cannot reach the inner leaf or the insulation. (b) The joists are carried on metal joist hangers fixed to the inner block leaf so they bear on the inner leaf without crossing the cavity. The floor build-up is: 225 mm x 50 mm timber joists, 20 mm plywood decking on top, then the tongued-and-grooved hardwood finished floor, with a plasterboard ceiling fixed beneath the joists and an airtight tape at the wall junction.',
