    gist: 'A wooden cut-string stairs is built from a string (250 × 50 mm), treads (250 × 25 mm), risers (175 × 20 mm), a newel post (110 × 110 mm), balusters (40 × 40 mm) and a handrail (60 × 60 mm), framing into a first-floor landing on 225 × 50 mm joists with a trimmer joist (225 × 75 mm). The 1:5 section (2022 HL Q7, 60 marks) wants the top three steps plus the landing drawn and LABELLED with the name and size of each member, and it specifically asks for two landing safety details. Most lost marks come from unlabelled members or omitting the two safety rules.',
