    gist: 'A domestic lighting circuit runs a 1.5 mm² twin-and-earth LSF (low-smoke-and-fume) cable from the distribution board to the switch, then loops on to the light points. The 2025 HL Q9 (60 marks) asks for the wiring layout with the correct cable SIZE and COLOUR CODING, plus two built-in safety features. Marks are lost when students omit the earth conductor, mislabel the cable colours, or give vague \'use good wiring\' safety points instead of named protective devices.',
