    gist: 'Timber-frame walls use TWO different moisture membranes, and the exam (worth ~15 marks) wants you to name each, place it correctly and explain the physics. The vapour control layer (VCL) goes on the warm, inner side to stop warm moist room air pushing water vapour into the structure; the breather membrane goes on the cold, outer side to let any trapped vapour escape while repelling rain. Get them the wrong way round and you describe a wall that traps moisture and rots.',
