    gist: 'A thermal (cold) bridge is a path of higher-conductivity material that bypasses the insulation, letting heat escape and creating a cold internal surface where condensation and mould form. At the flat-roof-to-wall abutment (~15 marks) the marks are won by showing CONTINUITY of insulation — the roof insulation and the full-fill cavity insulation must meet with no gap, and any blockwork crossing the line is replaced with a low-conductivity thermal block.',
