    focus: 'How a heat pump works and why its COP makes it efficient', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'On the short-answer question (Q8: explain any five terms, each worth 10 marks), \'explain a heat pump\' is a full 10-mark item, so you need real content, not one line. A heat pump moves heat from outside (air, ground or water) into the house using electricity, rather than burning fuel. The point that earns marks is the coefficient of performance (COP) of about 3-4: for every 1 unit of electricity it delivers 3-4 units of heat, which is why it is far more efficient than a fossil-fuel boiler and attracts grants.',
