      text: 'For every sound measure, finish with the named principle. \'215 mm concrete block on flat / precast concrete floor\' → HEAVINESS (high-density mass restricts vibration; insulation rises ~5 dB each time mass doubles). \'Airtight tape and full mortar joints, staggered plasterboard joints, sealed sockets\' → COMPLETENESS (any crack or hole dominates the sound leak). \'Acoustic mineral-wool panels / underlay\' → FLEXIBILITY (flexible material absorbs and dissipates sound energy). \'Cavity between leaves, argon gap in glazing, floating floor / room-within-a-room\' → ISOLATION (discontinuous construction converts sound at each junction, losing energy). Naming the word is worth a third of the marks on that part.',
