      modelAnswer: 'Composition: where the figure/focal point is placed (central or off-centre), how the figure fills the frame, what is in the foreground and background, whether the arrangement is balanced or weighted to one side, and what the eye is led to first. Colour: the main hues used, whether they are warm (reds, oranges, yellows) or cool (blues, greens), whether they are bright or muted/dull, any contrast between light and dark, and the mood the colours create (warm = cosy/lively, cool = calm/quiet). Each heading gets its own concrete, art-word description rather than a vague \'it looks nice\'.',
