    gist: 'The 2025 OL Q10 asked directly: how did Caravaggio create a sense of drama in his paintings? At OL you must refer to TWO named artworks. Caravaggio (c.1571-1610) builds drama mainly through chiaroscuro (strong contrast of light and dark) and tenebrism (figures lit by a single light source emerging from deep shadow), plus realistic, ordinary-looking figures and tightly cropped, close-up compositions that put the action right in front of the viewer. Good named works to use are \'The Calling of Saint Matthew\' (c.1599-1600) and \'Supper at Emmaus\' (1601). The exam rewards naming the technique and showing it in two specific works.',
