      text: 'A general \'he used dark and light\' answer stays in the Low band. Name two works and the device: in \'The Calling of Saint Matthew\' a single beam of light cuts across deep shadow to spotlight Matthew at the dramatic moment of his calling; in \'Supper at Emmaus\' bright light and a figure\'s outflung arm reaching toward the viewer freeze a moment of shock. Two named works + the named technique (chiaroscuro/tenebrism) is exactly what the \'two named artworks\' instruction demands.',
