    id: 'de-word-order-verb-second-fronting-ol',
    subjectId: 'german', topicId: 'german-1-3',
    subjectLabel: 'German', topicLabel: 'Writing About Your Experience',
    focus: 'Word order: when something else starts the sentence, the verb still comes SECOND (subject flips behind it)', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'German\'s core rule: the conjugated verb is ALWAYS the second idea in a main clause. So if you start with a time phrase, the subject must jump to AFTER the verb (inversion). \'Seit meiner letzten Prüfung ARBEITE ich fast jeden Tag\' (since my last exam I work almost every day) — verb \'arbeite\' is 2nd, \'ich\' follows it. In the Ordinary written-production letter task you slot phrases into a paragraph, and the verb-second pattern tells you which phrase fits. Writing \'Seit meiner Prüfung ich arbeite\' (English order) loses the mark.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Front phrase → verb 2nd → subject right after the verb',
      text: 'After a fronted phrase, flip subject and verb: \'Seit meiner letzten Prüfung ___\' is completed by \'arbeite ich\' (verb then subject), NOT \'ich arbeite\'. Count: idea 1 = the time phrase, idea 2 = the verb. The subject lands in third place.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'Ordinary written-production letter. Complete this sentence with the correct word order. Choose between \'arbeite ich\' and \'ich arbeite\' for the gap: \'Seit meiner letzten Prüfung im Juni ________ fast jeden Tag in einem Hotel.\' (meaning: \'Since my last exam in June I work almost every day in a hotel.\')',
      modelAnswer: 'arbeite ich — the sentence opens with a time phrase (\'Seit meiner letzten Prüfung im Juni\'), so the verb \'arbeite\' must be the second idea and the subject \'ich\' follows it. \'ich arbeite\' would push the verb to third place, which is wrong.',
      needed: ['Choose \'arbeite ich\' (verb before subject after a fronted phrase)', 'Reason: verb-second rule — fronted time phrase = idea 1, verb = idea 2, subject after'],
    },
    source: 'Topic Writing About Your Experience — SEC LC German 2025 OL, Schriftliche Produktion (a) letter gap-fill + marking scheme (\'arbeite ich\' inserted; St. = 4 x 1 mark)',
    marksWeight: 30,
