    id: 'de-word-order-damit-subordinate-clause-ol',
    subjectId: 'german', topicId: 'german-1-3',
    subjectLabel: 'German', topicLabel: 'Writing About Your Experience',
    focus: 'Word order in Written Production: after damit/weil the verb goes to the END', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'Written Production is marked on Communication AND Language, and the SEC scheme explicitly docks \'word order mistakes, esp. verb position\'. The most useful safe move is the subordinate-clause rule: after a joining word like \'damit\' (so that), \'weil\' (because) or \'dass\' (that), the verb is sent to the END of the clause. \'Das Geld kann ich sparen, DAMIT wir viel Spaß haben KÖNNEN\' (I can save the money so that we can have fun) — \'können\' sits right at the end. In the Ordinary letter task you build exactly this clause by slotting in \'damit wir\'.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'After damit/weil/dass, send the verb to the very end',
      text: 'Once you write \'damit\', \'weil\' or \'dass\', the verb of that clause must be LAST: \'..., damit wir viel Spaß haben KÖNNEN\' (with \'können\' at the end). A reliable mark-saver in the letter — but only if the verb actually lands last, not in second position.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'Ordinary letter, word order. Put the words in the correct German order to fill the clause after the comma (the clause means \'so that we can have a lot of fun\'): \'Das Geld kann ich sparen, ____________________.\' Words to arrange: damit / wir / viel Spaß / haben / können.',
      modelAnswer: '..., damit wir viel Spaß haben können. After the subordinating conjunction \'damit\', the finite verb \'können\' is pushed to the very end of the clause (with the infinitive \'haben\' just before it).',
      needed: ['Starts with \'damit wir\' (conjunction + subject)', 'Finite verb \'können\' placed LAST, after \'haben\' — verb-to-end after damit'],
    },
    source: 'Topic Writing About Your Experience — SEC LC German 2025 OL, Schriftliche Produktion (a) letter (\'..., damit wir viel Spaß haben können\') + 2025 HL marking scheme expression band (\'word order, esp. verb position\'); Written Production = 30 marks',
