    focus: 'Stating the modelling assumption that fixes the sign of every force when you formulate an equation of motion', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'The modelling cycle starts with formulation: turning a physical setup into an equation. The mark-losing step is almost never the calculus that follows it is getting the SIGNS of the forces right, and signs come straight from one assumption you must state: \'a resistive force always acts opposite to the direction of motion.\' When a particle is moving UPWARDS, gravity acts down AND air resistance acts down, so both enter the equation with the same (negative) sign. State that assumption out loud, take \'up\' as positive, and the equation writes itself.',
