    gist: 'A short-answer item can ask whether the Irish system of elections produces a government that is truly representative of the people, and to give one reason. Ireland uses PR-STV (Proportional Representation by Single Transferable Vote) in multi-seat constituencies, where you rank candidates 1, 2, 3 and the quota is reached by transferring surplus and eliminated votes - so seats roughly match each party\'s share of first-preference votes. Weak answers just say \'yes it is fair\' with no reason. You must name the system and give one real reason for your position.',
