    gist: 'A Section C discursive essay (100 marks) is marked across six components: Introduction (10), Knowledge (20), Evidence (20), Analysis & Synthesis (15), Evaluation (15) and Cohesion (20). The UDHR (Universal Declaration of Human Rights, adopted 1948) rests on the principle that rights are universal, inalienable and indivisible. When 2022 HL Q3(b) asks \'How universal is the UDHR? Discuss,\' the rubric explicitly demands contemporary examples plus the ideas of two theorists, at least one named on your course. Students lose the Evaluation marks by asserting \'rights are universal\' without weighing the counter-argument (cultural relativism, states that ignore it).',
