    gist: 'The Cluastuiscint LOVES numbers. The 2025 Higher Ceist 1 (15 mharc) packed five number-facts into one short píosa about a missing guide dog: missing \'le trí lá anuas\' (3 days), \'ceithre bliana d\'aois\' (age 4), stolen \'idir a sé agus a seacht a chlog tráthnóna Dé Sathairn seo caite\' (between 6 and 7 on Saturday evening), a \'duais €100\' reward, and a phone number to ring. Each was a 3-mharc answer. Students lose these marks because Irish numbers fly past in word form — if you try to translate in your head mid-play, you miss the next fact.',
