    gist: 'OL Ceist 5 (20 marc) gives you a fógra and asks for a teachtaireacht based on it — in 2024, inviting a friend to see Paul Mescal visiting your school. The top band (17-20) of the scheme requires \'cumas maith maidir leis na príomhghnéithe de cheart na teanga... briathra / ainmfhocail / aimsirí\'. Here\'s the secret: the fógra itself is a bank of perfect Irish, already in the right tense. The 2024 fógra said \'TABHARFAIDH an t-aisteoir Paul Mescal cuairt... BEIDH sé ag caint... FREAGRÓIDH sé ceisteanna\' — future tense, because the event hasn\'t happened yet. Reuse those exact verbs and your tenses can\'t go wrong.',
