    focus: 'Find the % rate: interest earned OVER the amount invested', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'If you know the start amount and the end amount, the interest earned is the difference (end minus start). To find the annual percentage interest rate, write that interest as a percentage of the amount INVESTED: (interest / amount invested) x 100. This is the reverse of finding the interest, and the exam likes to test it after a couple of straightforward interest parts.',
