      modelAnswer: '(a) Difference = total - shaded = (k+2)^2 - (k+3). Expand (k+2)^2 = k^2 + 4k + 4, so the difference = k^2 + 4k + 4 - k - 3 = k^2 + 3k + 1. Setting this equal to 271 gives k^2 + 3k + 1 = 271, as required. (b) Bring 271 across: k^2 + 3k + 1 - 271 = 0, i.e. k^2 + 3k - 270 = 0. Factorise: find two numbers with product -270 and sum +3, namely +18 and -15, so (k - 15)(k + 18) = 0. Then k - 15 = 0 or k + 18 = 0, giving k = 15 or k = -18. A pattern number can\'t be negative, so k = 15.',
