    focus: 'Grouped-data mean: use mid-interval values, write the numerator/denominator line first', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'When data is grouped into class intervals you cannot use the raw values, so you estimate the mean with the MID-INTERVAL value of each class (the average of its two endpoints). Multiply each mid-interval value by its frequency, add those products for the numerator, divide by the total frequency. The exam usually asks for the answer to a stated accuracy (e.g. nearest cm), and rounding correctly is itself a mark.',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Write the full (sum of mid x freq) / (total freq) line BEFORE simplifying',
      text: 'That single substituted line, e.g. [0(40)+2(120)+7(200)+12(280)+3(360)] / [0+2+7+12+3], is the High Partial Credit mark even if you slip in the arithmetic afterwards (the scheme awards HPC for \'first line in solution\'). Get a mid-interval wrong but stay consistent and finish, and you still score HPC. Drop or mis-round the final answer and you lose only Full Credit -1, so never skip the substitution line.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'Students\' long-jump distances are grouped: 0-80 cm: 0 students; 80-160 cm: 2; 160-240 cm: 7; 240-320 cm: 12; 320-400 cm: 3. Using mid-interval values, estimate the mean distance jumped, correct to the nearest centimetre.',
      modelAnswer: 'Mid-interval values (average of each interval\'s endpoints): 40, 120, 200, 280, 360. Mean = [0(40) + 2(120) + 7(200) + 12(280) + 3(360)] / (0 + 2 + 7 + 12 + 3) = [0 + 240 + 1400 + 3360 + 1080] / 24 = 6080 / 24 = 253.33... = 253 cm.',
      needed: ['Correct mid-interval values: 40, 120, 200, 280, 360 (average of each interval\'s endpoints)', 'Substituted line sum(mid x freq) over total frequency 24: 6080/24', 'Divide and round to the requested accuracy: 253.33... = 253 cm'],
    },
    source: 'Topic Summary statistics (averages & spread) — SEC JC Maths 2024 HL, Q2(d) + marking scheme (Scale 5C; HPC for \'first line in solution\'; LPC for one correct mid-interval value or indicating division by 24; Full Credit -1 for no/incorrect rounding)',
    marksWeight: 5,
