    id: 'jcmth-sample-space-product-even-complement-hl',
    subjectId: 'jc-mathematics', topicId: 'jc-mathematics-4-0',
    subjectLabel: 'Mathematics (Junior Cycle)', topicLabel: 'Counting & sample spaces',
    focus: 'Sample space of odd/even rolls: P(product even) via the all-odd complement', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'List the sample space systematically so none of the equally-likely outcomes are missed: three rolls each O or E gives 2 x 2 x 2 = 8 outcomes. A product of whole numbers is EVEN as long as at least one factor is even; it is ODD only when every factor is odd. So instead of hunting for all the \'even-product\' cases, count the single all-odd outcome (OOO) and subtract: P(even product) = 1 - P(all odd).',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Count the ONE all-odd outcome, then take the complement',
      text: 'Only OOO gives an odd product, so 7 of the 8 outcomes give an even product. P(product even) = 1 - 1/8 = 7/8. Listing and counting the seven even cases is slow and error-prone; the complement is one line. A correct numerator or denominator on its own earns Low Partial Credit, so even writing \'7/8\' partially is worth marks.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'A fair six-sided die is rolled three times; each roll is recorded as Odd (O) or Even (E). (a) Write the full sample space of O/E combinations. (b) Each outcome is equally likely. The three numbers rolled are multiplied together. Find the probability that the product is even.',
      modelAnswer: '(a) Sample space (2x2x2 = 8 outcomes): EEE, EEO, EOE, OEE, EOO, OEO, OOE, OOO. (b) A product is odd only when all three factors are odd, i.e. only OOO. So 8 - 1 = 7 outcomes give an even product. P(product even) = 7/8.',
      needed: ['List all 8 equally-likely O/E outcomes (2 x 2 x 2)', 'Recognise the product is odd only for OOO (all odd), so 7 of 8 give an even product', 'State the probability as 7/8'],
    },
    source: 'Topic Counting & sample spaces — SEC JC Maths 2023 HL, Q5(b)&(c) + marking scheme (Scale 15D; full credit answer 7/8; LPC for a correct numerator or denominator in (c))',
    marksWeight: 15,
