    focus: 'From a stem-and-leaf: mean = sum/n, median = middle value(s), range = max - min', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'A stem-and-leaf keeps every original value, so you can read all the data back off it in order. Mean = (sum of all values) / (number of values). Median = the middle value once they\'re in order; with an even count of n values, average the two middle ones (the n/2-th and the next). Range = largest - smallest. These three are separate marks, so attempt each even if one defeats you.',
