      label: 'Even number of values? Median is the AVERAGE of the two middle ones',
      text: 'With 12 values in order the median is between the 6th and 7th, so median = (6th + 7th) / 2. Picking just the 6th (or just the 7th) is the classic slip. Here the 6th = 189 and 7th = 190, so median = (189 + 190)/2 = 189.5 months. For the mean, write the sum-over-count line: relevant addition or identifying the right numbers already earns Low Partial Credit even before you divide.',
