    subjectId: 'jc-mathematics', topicId: 'jc-mathematics-4-1',
    subjectLabel: 'Mathematics (Junior Cycle)', topicLabel: 'Probability of random events',
    focus: 'Venn diagram probability: \'one or the other but not both\' = the two outside-the-overlap regions', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'Fill a two-set Venn diagram from the inside out: put the overlap (both) first, then subtract it from each set total to get the \'only\' regions, then place \'neither\' so all regions sum to the universal total. Probability = (favourable count) / (total). \'Plays sport OR computer games but NOT both\' means the two crescent regions only - the \'sport only\' part plus the \'computer games only\' part - never the overlap.',
