    subjectId: 'jc-mathematics', topicId: 'jc-mathematics-2-0',
    subjectLabel: 'Mathematics (Junior Cycle)', topicLabel: 'Measure, units & time',
    focus: 'Surface area of an open box: counting only the faces that exist and writing the correct cm^2 unit', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'Surface area is the total of every face, so the answer is an AREA and must be written in cm^2 (length is cm, area is cm^2, volume is cm^3). Two traps lose easy marks: an OPEN box has no top face, so you count 5 faces not 6; and forgetting the squared unit costs a mark on its own. Work face by face, double the matching pairs, then add. On this OL scale the units literally carry a mark, so always finish with cm^2.',
