    gist: 'In a fair test you control (keep the same) all the variables except the ones the investigation is actually about, so any change in the result can be linked to what you changed. The exam often gives a list of variables and asks you to pick three that should be KEPT CONSTANT and one that CHANGED during the investigation. Each correct pick is its own 3-mark item, so picking a variable that is irrelevant (e.g. \'loudness of noise in the room\') instead of a real constant is where students drop marks.',
