      text: 'Go down the list and label each variable: is it something you\'d hold the same (a control, e.g. concentration of acid, temperature of acid, total mass of chips), something that changes during the run (the chip size you vary, or the gas volume you measure), or something irrelevant (noise in the room)? The \'kept constant\' answers are the controls; the \'changed\' answer can be either the variable you deliberately vary (chip size) OR the measured outcome that changes over time (gas volume) — both are accepted here because the question asks what changed, not which is the independent variable.',
