      modelAnswer: '(i) Keep constant: the concentration of hydrochloric acid, the temperature of the acid, and the total mass of the marble chips (3 marks each). (ii) A relevant variable that changed: the size of the marble chips OR the volume of gas produced each minute — the SEC scheme accepts either, because both genuinely change during the investigation (the chip size is varied, the gas volume changes over time). \'Loudness of noise in the room\' is irrelevant and scores nothing.',
