      label: 'Tick a claim only if you can point to data on the graph that proves it',
      text: 'For every conclusion, ask \'can I point to data on THIS graph that shows it?\' Tick it only if the trend or values on the graph clearly back it up. Cross it if the graph trend is the opposite, if the claim is about a variable the experiment never measured (a \'healthier/better\' opinion is not in the data), OR if the graph simply doesn\'t show the comparison the claim makes (e.g. one line rising faster than another when they actually rise at about the same rate). Reasonable-sounding is not the same as data-supported.',
