      modelAnswer: 'Current assets = 21,600 + 20,000 + 25,000 = 66,600. Current liabilities = 14,000 + 7,000 = 21,000. Working capital = 66,600 − 21,000 = 45,600. The positive figure means the firm can cover its short-term debts.',
      needed: ['Total current assets = 66,600 (cash 21,600 + debtors 20,000 + closing stock 25,000)', 'Total current liabilities = 21,000 (creditors 14,000 + bank overdraft 7,000)', 'Working capital = 45,600 (current assets − current liabilities)'],
