    gist: 'A direct tax is charged directly on income or wealth (e.g. PAYE, USC, DIRT), paid straight to Revenue by the earner. An indirect tax is charged on spending and is built into the price of goods/services (e.g. VAT, excise duty, sugar tax); the seller collects it and passes it to the Government. The exam asks you to tick which type and then give a reason, so the tick alone is not enough, you must justify it.',
