      modelAnswer: '(a) Indirect tax. (b) An indirect tax is a tax on spending: it is levied on goods and is included in the price the consumer pays. The seller then collects this tax and sends it on to the Irish Government, so the sugar tax (charged on sugary drinks at the point of sale) is indirect.',
