      modelAnswer: 'Equilibrium occurs where quantity demanded = quantity supplied. That is at €400, where demand (600) equals supply (600). So the equilibrium price is €400 and the equilibrium quantity is 600,000 units (600 thousand). At every other price the quantities differ, so €400 is the only market-clearing price.',
