    gist: 'The trading account stops at Gross Profit. The profit & loss account is the missing link that turns Gross Profit into Net Profit. The rule is one line: Net Profit = Gross Profit + Gains − Expenses. Start from the Gross Profit figure carried down from the trading account, ADD any other income/gains (e.g. rent received, commission received), then SUBTRACT every running expense (wages, rent, insurance, light & heat, advertising, depreciation). Students lose marks by forgetting to add gains, by listing an expense in the wrong column so it isn\'t totalled, or by subtracting the expenses total from Sales instead of from Gross Profit. Add up ALL expenses first, then do Gross Profit + Gains − Total Expenses in one move.',
