      text: 'Write the Gross Profit figure first. List the gains under it and add them on. Total every expense in the inner column, carry the single total to the outer column, then subtract: Gross Profit + Gains − Total Expenses = Net Profit. Do the expenses subtotal before you subtract — one clean line beats six error-prone ones.',
