    gist: 'When a scenario person sets up their own business (e.g. Ted opening Healthy Ted Ltd) and you\'re asked to \'Explain one risk\', the marker rewards a NAMED risk plus an EXPLAINED consequence — not a vague worry. The SEC\'s accepted risks here are concrete: the owner may lose the money they invested if the business fails; they may not get suitable staff, which hurts sales/profits; their reputation could be damaged, hindering future projects; or they must work long hours, harming work/home balance. The single most common mark-loss is writing only the risk (\'it might fail\') with no effect. \'Explain\' = state the risk AND its knock-on impact.',
