      modelAnswer: 'One risk is that Ted may lose the money he has invested in the business if Healthy Ted Ltd fails — if sales are too low to cover costs, the business could close and Ted would not get back the capital he put in, leaving him with a financial loss and no income from it. (Other accepted risks, each with its effect: he may not be able to get suitable staff, which could lower service quality and reduce sales/profits; his reputation could be damaged if the business goes badly, which could hinder future projects; or he may have to work very long hours, which harms his work/home balance.) The key is to NAME one risk and then EXPLAIN the consequence with a \'so/which means…\' link, not just state the risk on its own.',
