    gist: 'Chronology means putting things in time order and naming time correctly. The trap students fall into is the century: the years in the 700s AD belong to the EIGHTH century (because the first 100 years, 1-100 AD, were the 1st century). To name the century of a year, take the first one or two digits and add one. The exam also asks you to count how many years or decades a timeline covers — just subtract the earlier date from the later one.',
