    id: 'jchist-cause-vs-consequence-before-after',
    subjectId: 'jc-history', topicId: 'jc-history-0-4',
    subjectLabel: 'History (Junior Cycle)', topicLabel: 'Cause and consequence',
    focus: 'Cause vs consequence: before the event, or after it?', level: 'common',
    gist: 'A CAUSE comes BEFORE an event and helps make it happen. A CONSEQUENCE comes AFTER an event and results from it. The exam asks you to define both terms and then to sort statements into \'cause\' or \'consequence\' columns. Marks are lost by mixing the direction — putting a result before the event, or a trigger after it. Test each statement: did this happen first and lead in (cause), or did it happen as a result later (consequence)?',
    oneMove: {
      label: 'Ask: did it lead IN (cause) or follow OUT (consequence)?',
      text: 'A cause comes before and brings the event about; a consequence comes after and results from it. For each statement, ask \'did this happen first and trigger it?\' = cause, or \'did this happen because of it, afterwards?\' = consequence. Anger at the abuses BEFORE the Reformation is a cause; wars of religion AFTER it are a consequence.',
    },
    check: {
      prompt: 'First: explain what \'cause\' and \'consequence\' mean in relation to a historical event. Then, for each statement about the Reformation in 16th-century Europe, say whether it is a CAUSE or a CONSEQUENCE: (1) There were abuses in the Catholic Church. (2) Wars of religion broke out in Europe. (3) The sale of indulgences angered some reformers. (4) The Council of Trent reformed the Catholic Church.',
      modelAnswer: 'A cause is something that happens BEFORE an event and helps to bring it about. A consequence is something that happens AFTER an event and results from it. (1) Abuses in the Catholic Church = CAUSE (they came first and led people to want reform). (2) Wars of religion broke out = CONSEQUENCE (they happened as a result of the religious split). (3) The sale of indulgences angering reformers = CAUSE (it angered Luther and others before the split). (4) The Council of Trent reformed the Catholic Church = CONSEQUENCE (it was the Church\'s response after the Reformation began).',
      needed: ['Defines cause as something coming BEFORE / leading to the event (3 marks)', 'Defines consequence as something coming AFTER / resulting from the event (3 marks)', 'Correctly sorts the statements: abuses = cause; wars of religion = consequence; indulgences angering reformers = cause; Council of Trent = consequence (3 marks each in the exam table)'],
    },
    source: 'Topic: Cause and consequence — SEC JC History 2025 CL, Q2(b) (define cause and consequence, 3m+3m) and Q2(c) (sort six statements: Cause, Consequence, Cause, Consequence, Consequence, Cause — 6x3m) + marking scheme.',
